{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793179292,"nonce":"mJo1Ni5Eo7Fw2NViKWAtkiRreMk=","message":"Final implementation and evidence:\n\nCached direct replay now returns pending meshes and GPU passes alongside primitive splices. Frame dispatch consumes those channels after 2D content; callbacks run once on successful replay, preserving per-frame viewports. Public primitive-only redraw returns false for other output. Equal primitive cursors use visit order. Existing conservative fallbacks remain.\n\nPrimitive-only perspective layers in ordered batches reuse the native bake path, keeping their projection frame independent of unrelated ordered content. An independent native scene is compared against collected-neighbor scenes across alpha .5,0,1,.75,.5 with two frames per stage, direct and compositor routes, including fractional bounds.\n\nFurther investigation found existing pool-dependent rasterization: native tight bakes and collected 3D bakes used requested dimensions although acquire() may return a larger pooled texture. Initial before/after snapshots therefore differed even after transition stability was fixed. Do not claim bit-exact baseline 3D edge parity. Oversized-pool negative control: feature (162,18) [95,24,93,255] vs fresh-reference [204,51,26,255], both routes. Raster uniforms, glyph clipping and source UVs now use the allocated extent in both bake paths. The final independent native/pool controls pass. Initial geometry-padding and guard-texel experiments were removed in favor of the native perspective path.\n\nFinal scoped normal checks: 46 app tests (eight new release-boundary, five layer-text including projection unit test, six retained canvas, nine cross-stream, ten effect/blend groups, eight RGBA ordering) and 20 GPU tests (six overlay unit, three composite-layer, seven producer opacity, four RGBA ordering). All eight new cases also pass with both storage flags temporarily disabled for DT. Source restored byte-for-byte; restored normal matrix passes. Touched-file rustfmt and diff checks pass. CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 throughout; capacities 1024; no source edits during builds, broad gates, desktop input or push.\n\nLogs /private/tmp/blinc-release-final-{matrix,layer-text,retained,cross,effects,rgba,gpu-overlay,gpu-composite,gpu-producer,gpu-rgba,dt,restored}.log. Baseline negatives /private/tmp/blinc-release-matrix-baseline-gpu.log; oversized-pool negative /private/tmp/blinc-release-pool-negative.log.\n\nCosts: replay retains Arc-backed mesh data and GPU-pass handles already emitted by callbacks, not copied mesh geometry. Perspective native bakes reuse the existing bounded texture pool. Allocated-extent mapping changes raster/source coordinates, not pool policy. No timing or device-memory benchmark, mobile/browser pixel claim, public API or shader/primitive ABI change.\n\nThis closes the confirmed mixed-boundary regression and cached-output defects. It does not establish general isolation of meshes/custom passes inside opacity/effect groups, arbitrary nested 3D composition or named native Sample support. Parent e0a7502 stays open for those architectural ownership gaps and legacy collection isolation. Release packaging is separately tracked by 7d752335eda4def69132bdfb800c99c8b1c6ac2d05eccf357b74b6496eb687eb; tree/window queue isolation remains 3d90a31.","files":null}]}